From 36e7aaeaf08b46f0ecd0c624ca640b3567d927ef Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Andree Toonk <andree@toonk.io>
Date: Sun, 6 Sep 2026 19:16:07 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 08/13] tcp: link backpressure, and a zero-window probe that is
 not a loss

tcp.LinkBackpressure treats a link's WouldBlock on write as "not sent, try
again when told": the attempt is undone, the endpoint joins a per-stack
line and stops sending; tcp.ResumeBlocked gives the line a turn each,
tcp.LinkTurn segments, in order. Upstream advances SND.NXT whether or not
the link took the segment, so a full link can only drop, and with 2000
connections behind one queue the drops became RTO storms.
tcp.SeparateZeroWindowProbe sends the probe on the retransmit timer
without counting a timeout or collapsing the window. tcp.PreciseRTT
measures the round trip from the local clock even when the peer echoes a
TCP timestamp, which carries only milliseconds. tcp.ProcessorCount sets
how many processor goroutines a stack starts. A sent segment that carries
the delayed ACK disarms its timer.
---
 pkg/tcpip/transport/tcp/endpoint.go | 137 +++++++++++++++++
 pkg/tcpip/transport/tcp/protocol.go |  17 ++-
 pkg/tcpip/transport/tcp/snd.go      | 221 +++++++++++++++++++++++++---
 3 files changed, 353 insertions(+), 22 deletions(-)

